## Assembler Features
- [X] Macro support - Define reusable code patterns with `.macro`/`.endmacro`
- [X] Conditional assembly - `.ifdef`/`.endif` directives (asm20), `define:label` command line
- [X] More instructions - All standard 6502 opcodes present in instruction tables
- [ ] Better error messages - Include source line content in error output, not just line numbers
- [ ] `.ifndef` directive - complement to `.ifdef`
- [ ] `.else` for conditionals - more expressive conditional assembly
- [ ] `.fill count, value` - emit N copies of a byte, useful for padding/alignment
- [ ] `.align N` - align PC to N-byte boundary (emits padding)
- [ ] More expression operators - `*`, `/`, `&`, `|`, `^` for bit manipulation
- [ ] `.incbin "file"` - include raw binary data
- [ ] `.repeat N` / `.endrepeat` - unroll loops at assembly time
- [ ] Anonymous labels (`+`, `-`) - for short forward/backward branches without naming
- [ ] Enhance `define:` to support optional values - e.g. `define:LABEL=$1234`
- [ ] Should not silently accept expressions with spaces and ignore values - `x = a + b` currently means `x = a`
- [ ] Improve error message when parsing values - currently says "invalid opcode" which is misleading for `.data` or assignments

